  "review": [
    "Read all eight setup helper modules and eight tests. First-party code and explicitly synthetic identities, dates, source UUIDs, example room authority, model/rate labels and game projections; no real account, credential, local file contents or third-party assets.",
    "Six modules re-export shared projections; pairing facts also hashes opaque references with Web Crypto. Shared implementations remain separate unexported dependencies; passing these tests does not clear their source for publication.",
    "Pairing preparation matches owner-reviewed revision and remaining finite lease, selected exact task/chat, admitted optional sibling, installation and MCP-client hashes, and a nonambiguous registered destination. Existing endpoint remains responsible for fresh account/device/contract validation.",
    "Discord apply verifies exact local source grants and current contract approval before mutations, rejects a changed all-approved snapshot, reads only selected exact chats, saves a bounded resume selection and retires its temporary publishing revision. The existing publisher owns baseline and delivery; this helper does not publish text.",
    "Fixed a malformed-expiry acceptance gap: the selection receipt must have an expiry strictly later than now, which rejects both expired values and Date.parse NaN before resume-save. Reproduced the failed boundary test before the one-line correction.",
    "Fixture tests distinguish room membership from live presence, pairing from execution authority, player identity from action lease/connector readiness, and bounded own-key budget from generic native allowance. No actual grant, paid run or game action occurs."
